  "body": "### Summary\nAs the fixture steward, I want `anonymize.py check` to refuse any element but `br` and the clear `div` inside a redacted `span.signature`, so that the check verifies what `tooling/fixtures/README.md:70` says (\"nothing else\") independently of the redactor (LESSONS 33-34).\n\n### Scope\n- `tooling/fixtures/anonymize.py` `SIGNATURE_TEXT_RE` is text-only: a span holding ``'&lt;img … alt=…&gt;'`` or a link around the placeholder passes `check` today (Fable probe on #764, finding 2). The redactor never emits it.\n- Also from #764 finding 1: one member handle in free prose of `R267a` stays in clear (already public on dev-swift in `P03m` and `R122d`); `R20`, the same page, aliased it. Add it to `extra_pseudos` and republish the three captures from the Mac, or record the best-effort decision. Do not quote the handle in public text.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- New `check` tests: an `img`, an `a`, any element other than `br`/clear `div` in a signature span fails; the corpus still passes.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
